,"followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-07T06:55:12Z","updated_at":"2025-06-08T09:30:47Z","body":"This is actually intentional. Hidden objects are not physics interpolated in order to save processing. Consider a whole branch may be hidden and moved via a parent, calculating all their interpolated xforms would in most cases be extremely wasteful.\n\nEDIT:\nThinking about it I can see some situations where this would be really handy, rather than working around by using unhidden `Node3D`. This wasn't an obvious use case.\n\nI think this can likely be done by calculating such hidden chains on demand, it may not be hugely involved. I'll have a look tommorrow / monday. It won't be as cheap as unhidden nodes, but should be user transparent.\n\n> Likely a duplicate of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107142?\n\nNo, these are quite different issues (although they both concern hidden objects). #107142 should be fixed with #107175 .","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2951981228/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]